# EXAMPLE ONLY. Nothing here is installed. To use it the OWNER must (see infra/sentinel/README.md and DESIGN.md section 4):
#   1. confirm the repository is PUBLIC (scheduled Actions minutes are free only for public repositories; a private repo draws on a quota),
#   2. copy this file to  .github/workflows/aicc-sentinel.yml  and merge it into the DEFAULT branch (GitHub runs `schedule:` only from the default branch),
#   3. add two repository secrets (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions > New repository secret): TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN and TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.
#      Without them the job still runs and checks, but only writes the log (Telegram stays disabled).
#
# Honest expectations
#   * GitHub does not promise the schedule. "*/10" is best effort: runs are often delayed by several minutes at busy times and can be dropped.
#     A 5-minute cron is allowed but no more reliable, so this uses 10. Treat detection time as "roughly 20-40 minutes", not "within a minute".
#   * GitHub DISABLES scheduled workflows in a public repository after 60 days without repository activity (a commit, issue, PR...). Re-enable it in the Actions tab,
#     or keep the repo active. A silent observer looks exactly like a healthy one: check the Actions tab now and then.
#   * State (the N-of-M window and the cooldown) is kept between runs with the Actions cache. If GitHub evicts the cache (7 days unused, or 10 GB repo limit) the window
#     simply restarts empty: that can delay a DOWN by a couple of runs but cannot create a false one.
#   * Each run saves a new tiny cache entry (cache keys are immutable). They age out by themselves.
#
# Supply chain
#   * The workflow checks out THIS repository only to run infra/sentinel/sentinel.py (standard library, no installs). Anyone who can push to the default branch can change
#     what runs next to the Telegram secrets: keep branch protection on, never trigger this on pull_request/pull_request_target or forks, and never add a step that runs
#     code from a pull request. Secrets are not exposed to workflows from forks.
#   * The `uses:` lines below carry well-known MAJOR tags because a full commit SHA cannot be looked up offline. Before enabling, pin each to the full 40-character SHA of
#     the current release (a tag can be moved; a SHA cannot) and add Dependabot for github-actions so the pins are refreshed.
#   * The secrets reach the process only through `env:` (never in `run:` text, arguments or logs). sentinel.py reads TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN / TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID from the environment.
#   * targets.stage.toml is public in a public repo. It contains no credential; it does contain the staging identity id, which is an identifier (not an authentication secret).
name: aicc-sentinel
on:
  schedule:
    - cron: "*/10 * * * *"
  workflow_dispatch: {}
permissions:
  contents: read
concurrency:
  group: aicc-sentinel
  cancel-in-progress: false
jobs:
  check:
    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04            # ships Python 3.12; nothing is installed
    timeout-minutes: 3
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4   # PIN TO A FULL COMMIT SHA before enabling
        with:
          persist-credentials: false
          sparse-checkout: infra/sentinel
      - uses: actions/cache/restore@v4   # PIN TO A FULL COMMIT SHA before enabling
        with:
          path: .sentinel-state
          key: sentinel-state-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}
          restore-keys: sentinel-state-
      - name: Probe
        env:
          # repository secrets; never echo them, never put them in run: text or arguments
          TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN }}
          TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID: ${{ secrets.TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID }}
        run: |
          python3 --version
          # A 10-minute cadence needs a shorter window than the Mac profile: DOWN after 2 of the last 3 runs failed (one blip never pages).
          # Add --fail-on-down if you also want a failed run (and GitHub's own email) while a target is down; it repeats every run, so it is off by default.
          python3 infra/sentinel/sentinel.py \
            --config infra/sentinel/targets.stage.toml \
            --once --quiet-ok \
            --state-file .sentinel-state/state.json \
            --host-label github-actions \
            --fail-n 2 --window-m 3
      - uses: actions/cache/save@v4   # PIN TO A FULL COMMIT SHA before enabling
        if: always()                  # save the state even when a step above failed
        with:
          path: .sentinel-state
          key: sentinel-state-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}
